WEBVTT

00:00:42.924 --> 00:00:46.691
I can't believe we
actually bought this thing.

00:00:46.724 --> 00:00:49.324
There's a reason charity
auctions have an open bar.

00:00:49.357 --> 00:00:51.257
Don't you think...

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.390
I don't know, it's kind of creepy?

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.457
It's okay.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.958
I'll keep you safe.

00:01:01.058 --> 00:01:03.390
Maybe you're the one i
ought to be scared of.

00:01:05.457 --> 00:01:08.557
Mmm. Let's go upstairs.

00:01:08.591 --> 00:01:11.691
Give me 10 minutes to lock up.

00:01:11.724 --> 00:01:13.591
Mmm.

00:01:13.624 --> 00:01:15.123
Make than one minute.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:07.958
If you don't hurry up, i'm
gonna start without you!

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.891
Babe, get the lights.
I can't see a thing.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.857
Do you smell something?

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:41.991
Ann?

00:02:44.657 --> 00:02:46.190
Ann?!

00:03:04.757 --> 00:03:07.357

...3-4-2-0.

00:03:08.424 --> 00:03:10.490
All right. You're in there.

00:03:10.524 --> 00:03:11.624
Perfect.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:14.390
So, is that brandi with a "y" or an "i"?

00:03:31.891 --> 00:03:34.924
All right, listen. I got to go.

00:03:34.958 --> 00:03:37.058
Hold that thought. I'll
be right back, okay?

00:03:39.123 --> 00:03:41.757
All right, so, i think i got
something. Oh, yeah, me too.

00:03:41.791 --> 00:03:43.724
I think we need to take
a little shore leave

00:03:43.757 --> 00:03:45.791
For just a little bit.
What do you think, huh?

00:03:45.824 --> 00:03:47.457
I'm so in the door with this one here.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.891
So, what are we today,
dean? Are we rock stars?

00:03:49.924 --> 00:03:51.223
Are we army rangers?

00:03:51.257 --> 00:03:53.924
We're l.A. Tv scouts looking
for people with special skills.

00:03:55.024 --> 00:03:57.058
But, hey, it's not that far off, right?

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.791
By the way, she's got
a friend over there.

00:03:59.824 --> 00:04:01.657
I can probably hook you
up. What do you think?

00:04:01.691 --> 00:04:03.424
Dean, uh, no thanks.
I can get my own dates.

00:04:03.457 --> 00:04:05.524
Yeah, you can, but you don't.

00:04:05.557 --> 00:04:07.591
What is that supposed to mean?

00:04:07.624 --> 00:04:09.324
Nothing. What do you got?

00:04:09.357 --> 00:04:11.891
Mark and ann telesca
of new paltz, new york,

00:04:11.924 --> 00:04:14.991
Were both found dead in their
home just a few days ago.

00:04:15.024 --> 00:04:16.857
Throats were slit, there were no prints,

00:04:16.891 --> 00:04:18.657
No murder weapons, all
- Dean?

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.958
No prints, no murder weapons,

00:04:19.991 --> 00:04:21.958
All doors and windows were
locked from the inside.

00:04:21.991 --> 00:04:24.058
Could just be a garden-Variety murder.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.390
You know, not our department.
No, dad says different.

00:04:26.424 --> 00:04:27.457
What do you mean?

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.457
Look.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:29.657
Dad noted three murders

00:04:29.691 --> 00:04:31.591
In the same area of upstate new york.

00:04:31.624 --> 00:04:34.157
First one, right here, 1912.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:37.958
The second one in 1945,
and the third in 1970.

00:04:37.991 --> 00:04:40.524
The same m.O. As the telescas
- The throats were slit,

00:04:40.557 --> 00:04:42.324
The houses were locked from the inside.

00:04:42.357 --> 00:04:43.891
So much time passed between the murders

00:04:43.924 --> 00:04:45.724
That nobody checked the
pattern except for dad.

00:04:45.757 --> 00:04:47.757
He always kept his eyes
peeled for another one.

00:04:47.791 --> 00:04:49.123
And now we got one. Exactly.

00:04:49.157 --> 00:04:51.357
All right. I'm with you.
It's worth checking out.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.624
We can't pick this up till
first thing, though, right?

00:04:53.657 --> 00:04:55.958
Yeah. Good.

00:04:55.991 --> 00:04:57.457
Dean...

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:58.924
Ladies. Did you miss me?

00:04:58.958 --> 00:05:00.624
I'm just kidding.

00:05:00.657 --> 00:05:03.490
Listen, i talked to my
producer, and it is looking good.

00:05:19.958 --> 00:05:21.857
Oh, man, that's so not cool.

00:05:21.891 --> 00:05:25.357
I just swept the telesca
house with the emf. It's clean.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:28.024
And last night, while you were...

00:05:28.058 --> 00:05:29.290
Out...

00:05:29.324 --> 00:05:30.624
Oh, good times.

00:05:30.657 --> 00:05:32.290
...i checked the history of the house.

00:05:32.324 --> 00:05:33.924
No hauntings, no violent crimes,

00:05:33.958 --> 00:05:36.457
Nothing strange about the
telescas themselves, either.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:38.791
So if it's not the people
and it's not the house,

00:05:38.824 --> 00:05:40.390
Then maybe it's the contents -

00:05:40.424 --> 00:05:42.591
A cursed object or
something. House is clean.

00:05:42.624 --> 00:05:43.991
You said that.

00:05:44.024 --> 00:05:45.024
No, i mean it's empty.

00:05:45.058 --> 00:05:47.058
No furniture, nothing.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.390
Where's all their stuff?

00:06:17.424 --> 00:06:20.524
Silent auctions, estate sales -

00:06:20.557 --> 00:06:23.190
It's like a garage sale for
w.A.S.P.S, if you ask me.

00:06:23.223 --> 00:06:24.557
Can i help you, gentlemen?

00:06:27.223 --> 00:06:30.090
I'd like some champagne, please.

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.857
He's not a waiter.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.424
I'm sam connors.

00:06:38.457 --> 00:06:41.058
This is my brother, dean.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.223
We are art dealers with connors limited.

00:06:43.257 --> 00:06:45.190
You're art dealers? That's right.

00:06:45.223 --> 00:06:47.624
I'm daniel blake. This
is my auction house.

00:06:47.657 --> 00:06:50.824
Now, gentlemen, this
is a private showing,

00:06:50.857 --> 00:06:53.757
And i don't remember seeing
you on the guest list.

00:06:53.791 --> 00:06:55.090
We're there, chuckles.

00:06:55.123 --> 00:06:57.290
You just need to take another look.

00:06:57.324 --> 00:06:58.724
Oh, finally.

00:07:01.257 --> 00:07:02.524
Cheers.

00:07:20.591 --> 00:07:23.791
A fine example of american
primitive, wouldn't you say?

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:32.691
Well, i'd say it's more
grant wood than grandma moses

00:07:34.324 --> 00:07:35.757
But you knew that.

00:07:35.791 --> 00:07:37.424
You just wanted to see if i did.

00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:39.257
Guilty.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:41.958
And clumsy. I apologize.

00:07:41.991 --> 00:07:43.924
I'm sarah blake.

00:07:43.958 --> 00:07:46.524
I'm sam.

00:07:46.557 --> 00:07:50.991
This is my...brother, dean.

00:07:51.024 --> 00:07:52.424
Dean. Hmm.

00:07:52.457 --> 00:07:54.090
Can we get you some more mini quiche?

00:07:54.123 --> 00:07:56.657
Mnh-Mnh, i'm good. Thanks.

00:07:56.691 --> 00:07:59.123
So, can i help you with something?

00:07:59.157 --> 00:08:01.490
Yeah, actually.

00:08:01.524 --> 00:08:04.357
What can you tell us
about the telesca estate?

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.557
The whole thing's pretty
grisly if you ask me,

00:08:06.591 --> 00:08:08.557
Selling their things this soon.

00:08:08.591 --> 00:08:10.691
But dad's right about one thing -

00:08:10.724 --> 00:08:12.958
Sensationalism brings out the crowds.

00:08:12.991 --> 00:08:15.424
Even the rich ones.

00:08:18.223 --> 00:08:20.290
Is it possible to see the provenances?

00:08:20.324 --> 00:08:24.123
I'm afraid there isn't
any chance of that.

00:08:24.157 --> 00:08:26.123
Why not?

00:08:26.157 --> 00:08:27.724
You're not on the guest list...

00:08:27.757 --> 00:08:29.290
And i think it's time to leave.

00:08:29.324 --> 00:08:31.324
Well, we don't have to be
told twice. Apparently, you do.

00:08:31.357 --> 00:08:32.390
Okay, it's all right.

00:08:32.424 --> 00:08:35.290
We don't want any trouble. We'll go.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:44.457
Dad, that was rude.

00:08:47.357 --> 00:08:49.791
Grant wood, grandma moses
- What?

00:08:49.824 --> 00:08:51.157
Art history course.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:52.757
It's good for meeting girls.

00:08:52.791 --> 00:08:54.591
It's like i don't even know you.

00:09:11.591 --> 00:09:12.691
Huh.Huh.

00:09:12.724 --> 00:09:14.891
And what was the providence?

00:09:14.924 --> 00:09:16.024
Provenance.

00:09:16.058 --> 00:09:17.490
It's a certificate of origin,

00:09:17.524 --> 00:09:18.857
Like a biography, you know?

00:09:18.891 --> 00:09:21.123
We can use them to track
the history of the pieces,

00:09:21.157 --> 00:09:22.857
See if anything's got a freaky past.

00:09:22.891 --> 00:09:25.223
We're not getting
anything out of chuckles,

00:09:25.257 --> 00:09:26.691
But, uh, sarah... yeah.

00:09:26.724 --> 00:09:28.591
Maybe you can get her
to write it on a napkin.

00:09:28.624 --> 00:09:30.024
Not me.

00:09:30.058 --> 00:09:31.424
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:09:31.457 --> 00:09:33.123
Pickups are your thing, dean.

00:09:33.157 --> 00:09:35.290
It wasn't my butt she was checking out.

00:09:35.324 --> 00:09:38.624
In other words, you want me
to use her to get information.

00:09:38.657 --> 00:09:40.190
Sometimes you got to
take one for the team.

00:09:40.223 --> 00:09:42.724
Call sarah.

00:09:47.058 --> 00:09:48.490
Nice place.

00:09:48.524 --> 00:09:49.624
Yeah.

00:09:57.991 --> 00:09:59.090
Glad you called.

00:10:00.157 --> 00:10:02.324
Surprised, but glad.

00:10:02.357 --> 00:10:03.390
Yeah?

00:10:03.424 --> 00:10:05.223
Although you seemed to have a hard time

00:10:05.257 --> 00:10:07.624
Getting out the words, "would
you like to have dinner?"

00:10:07.657 --> 00:10:09.724
Yeah.

00:10:09.757 --> 00:10:12.924
I haven't really been
on a date in a while.

00:10:12.958 --> 00:10:14.390
Welcome to the club.

00:10:14.424 --> 00:10:16.857
You're kidding me.

00:10:16.891 --> 00:10:20.657
Man: here we are.

00:10:20.691 --> 00:10:22.290
The wine list.

00:10:35.691 --> 00:10:40.424
I don't know about romeo
here, but i'll have a beer.

00:10:42.724 --> 00:10:43.757
And you?

00:10:43.791 --> 00:10:45.090
I will, too.

00:10:45.123 --> 00:10:46.157
Certainly.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:48.524
Sam: so, you studied art in school, huh?

00:10:48.557 --> 00:10:49.591
Sarah: it's true.

00:10:49.624 --> 00:10:50.691
I was an artist -

00:10:50.724 --> 00:10:54.657
A terrible, terrible artist.

00:10:54.691 --> 00:10:56.657
That's why i'm in the auction business.

00:10:56.691 --> 00:10:58.190
And you were pre-Law?

00:10:58.223 --> 00:10:59.290
Yeah.

00:10:59.324 --> 00:11:02.290
But you didn't go to
law school. How come?

00:11:02.324 --> 00:11:06.024
Uh, it's a really long
story for another time.

00:11:06.058 --> 00:11:08.657
You're not like any art
dealer i've ever met.

00:11:13.757 --> 00:11:16.058
So...what did you mean when you said

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:17.724
You hadn't been on a date in a while?

00:11:17.757 --> 00:11:19.490
Trying to make me feel
like i'm not such a loser?

00:11:19.524 --> 00:11:21.223
I'm sure many things, sam.

00:11:21.257 --> 00:11:24.390
I'm also sure "loser" isn't one of them.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:31.490
It was my mom.

00:11:31.524 --> 00:11:33.757
She died about a year ago.

00:11:33.791 --> 00:11:36.357
Totally unexpected.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:39.824
It really threw me.

00:11:41.524 --> 00:11:47.190
I went into this shell
- A nice, warm, safe shell.

00:11:47.223 --> 00:11:49.991
But lately, i've been thinking...

00:11:50.024 --> 00:11:53.624
It's not what she would
have wanted for me.

00:11:53.657 --> 00:11:55.123
So...

00:12:00.257 --> 00:12:01.557
So, what about you?

00:12:01.591 --> 00:12:04.290
You're a reasonably attractive guy.

00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:07.691
Reasonably.

00:12:07.724 --> 00:12:10.891
Why haven't you been out and about?

00:12:19.123 --> 00:12:22.824
Another long story for another time.

00:12:28.991 --> 00:12:30.857
So, she just handed the
providences over to you?

00:12:30.891 --> 00:12:32.058
Provenances.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:34.924
Provenances? Yes, we
went back to her place.

00:12:34.958 --> 00:12:37.257
I got a copy of the papers.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:38.757
And?

00:12:38.791 --> 00:12:42.024
And nothing. That's it. I left.

00:12:42.058 --> 00:12:46.424
You didn't have to con her
or do any special favors?

00:12:46.457 --> 00:12:48.457
Would you get your mind
out of the gutter, please?

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.991
When this whole thing's done,
we could stick around a bit.

00:12:51.024 --> 00:12:52.757
Why? So you could take her out again.

00:12:52.791 --> 00:12:54.624
It's obvious you're into
her. Even i can see that.

00:12:54.657 --> 00:12:56.924
Hey, all right. I think
i got something here.

00:13:01.157 --> 00:13:02.958
"Portrait of isaiah merchant's family,

00:13:02.991 --> 00:13:04.324
Painted 1910."

00:13:04.357 --> 00:13:06.424
Now compare the names of the
owners with dad's journal.

00:13:10.724 --> 00:13:14.490
"First purchased in 1912 to peter sims."

00:13:14.524 --> 00:13:16.724
Peter sims murdered, 1912.

00:13:20.791 --> 00:13:23.424
Same thing in 1945.

00:13:23.457 --> 00:13:25.958
Oh, same thing in 1970.

00:13:25.991 --> 00:13:27.223
Then stored,

00:13:27.257 --> 00:13:29.591
Until it was donated to a
charity auction last month,

00:13:29.624 --> 00:13:31.490
Where the telescas bought it.

00:13:31.524 --> 00:13:34.190
So, what do you think?
It's haunted or cursed?

00:13:34.223 --> 00:13:36.390
Either way, it's toast.

00:13:58.757 --> 00:14:00.324
Go ahead.

00:14:45.058 --> 00:14:46.424
Ugly-Ass thing.

00:14:46.457 --> 00:14:49.324
If you ask me, we're doing
the art world a favor.

00:15:18.974 --> 00:15:21.240
We got a problem. I
can't find my wallet.

00:15:21.974 --> 00:15:23.741
How's that my problem?

00:15:23.774 --> 00:15:27.108
'Cause i think i dropped it
in the warehouse last night.

00:15:27.141 --> 00:15:28.141
You're kidding, right?

00:15:28.174 --> 00:15:29.874
I mean, it's got my prints, my i.D. -

00:15:29.907 --> 00:15:31.974
Well, my fake i.D.,
anyway, but we got to get it

00:15:32.007 --> 00:15:33.807
Before somebody else finds it. Come on.

00:15:44.074 --> 00:15:46.141
How do you lose your wallet, dean?

00:15:47.907 --> 00:15:49.741
Hey, guys.

00:15:49.774 --> 00:15:52.041
Sarah. Hey.

00:15:52.074 --> 00:15:53.640
What are you doing here?

00:15:53.674 --> 00:15:55.874
Oh...

00:15:55.907 --> 00:15:57.240
We're
- We're leaving town,

00:15:57.273 --> 00:15:59.373
And, you know, we came to say goodbye.

00:15:59.407 --> 00:16:01.208
What are you talking about, sam?

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:04.041
We're sticking around for
at least another day or two.

00:16:04.074 --> 00:16:05.607
Oh, sam, by the way,

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:09.041
I wanted to give you
that 20 bucks i owe you.

00:16:09.074 --> 00:16:12.373
I always forget.

00:16:12.407 --> 00:16:14.474
There you go.

00:16:17.174 --> 00:16:18.974
Well, i'll leave you
two crazy kids alone.

00:16:19.007 --> 00:16:21.607
I got to go do... something...somewhere.

00:16:28.841 --> 00:16:30.741
So...

00:16:30.774 --> 00:16:32.141
I had a good time last night.

00:16:32.174 --> 00:16:34.174
Yeah. Yeah, i did, too.

00:16:34.208 --> 00:16:37.174
Maybe we should do it again sometime?

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.741
You know, i'd love to, i really would,

00:16:41.774 --> 00:16:43.574
But dean
- He was just screwing around.

00:16:43.607 --> 00:16:45.841
We really are taking off today.

00:16:45.874 --> 00:16:48.041
Oh. Oh.

00:16:48.074 --> 00:16:49.474
Now that's too bad.

00:16:49.507 --> 00:16:52.307
Oh, my god! What?

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:53.741
The -

00:16:53.774 --> 00:16:55.373
That painting...

00:16:55.407 --> 00:16:57.607
Looks so good.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:17:00.941
If you can call that monstrosity good,

00:17:00.974 --> 00:17:02.707
Then, yeah, i guess.

00:17:02.741 --> 00:17:04.741
Sarah, what do you know
about that painting?

00:17:04.774 --> 00:17:06.974
Not much. Just that it creeps me out.

00:17:07.007 --> 00:17:08.440
We sold it to the telescas

00:17:08.474 --> 00:17:10.440
At a charity auction the
night they were murdered.

00:17:10.474 --> 00:17:12.974
And now you're just gonna sell it again?

00:17:13.007 --> 00:17:15.907
As much as my dad wants
to, no. I won't let him.

00:17:15.941 --> 00:17:17.874
I think it'd be in bad taste.

00:17:17.907 --> 00:17:19.674
Good, yeah. You know what? Don't. Don't.

00:17:19.707 --> 00:17:21.307
Make sure you don't, okay? Why?

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:23.407
Don't tell me you're interested in that.

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:25.273
No, god, no. Not in buying it, no.

00:17:25.307 --> 00:17:27.874
I got to go. I got to
take care of something.

00:17:27.907 --> 00:17:29.440
But, um, i will call you back.

00:17:29.474 --> 00:17:31.007
I will call you. I'll see you later.

00:17:31.041 --> 00:17:33.373
Wait, so you're not leaving tonight?

00:17:33.407 --> 00:17:36.874
No, i guess not. I'll see you.

00:17:38.874 --> 00:17:40.741
Okay.

00:17:42.841 --> 00:17:45.841
I don't understand, dean.
We burned the damn thing.

00:17:45.874 --> 00:17:47.941
Yeah, thank you, captain obvious.

00:17:47.974 --> 00:17:51.907
We just need to figure out
another way to get rid of it.

00:17:51.941 --> 00:17:53.041
Any ideas?

00:17:53.074 --> 00:17:54.307
Okay, all right.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:56.807
Well, um, in almost all the
lore about haunted paintings,

00:17:56.841 --> 00:17:58.574
It's always the painting's
subject that haunts them.

00:17:58.607 --> 00:18:00.373
Yeah? All right.

00:18:00.407 --> 00:18:02.874
So we need to figure out
everything there is to know

00:18:02.907 --> 00:18:05.640
About that creepy-Ass family
in that creepy-Ass painting.

00:18:05.674 --> 00:18:07.774
What were their names again?

00:18:08.807 --> 00:18:10.108
The isaiah merchant family, right?

00:18:10.141 --> 00:18:11.907
Yeah, that's right.

00:18:11.941 --> 00:18:15.407
I dug up every scrap of
local history i could find.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:17.440
So, uh, are you boys crime buffs?

00:18:17.474 --> 00:18:20.407
Kind of. Why do you ask?

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:21.774
Well...

00:18:25.373 --> 00:18:27.307
Yes. Yeah, that sounds about right.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:28.907
The whole family was killed?

00:18:28.941 --> 00:18:31.674
It seems this isaiah, he
slits his kids' throats,

00:18:31.707 --> 00:18:33.707
Then his wife, then himself.

00:18:33.741 --> 00:18:37.507
Now, he was a barber by
trade. Used a straight razor.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.307
Why'd he do it?

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:41.607
Well, let's look.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.640
Uh, "people who knew
him described isaiah

00:18:43.674 --> 00:18:45.607
"As having a stern
and harsh temperament,

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:47.307
And controlled his
family with an iron fist."

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:52.108
Wife, two sons, adopted daughter
- Yeah, yeah.

00:18:52.141 --> 00:18:54.574
There were whispers that the
wife was gonna take the kids

00:18:54.607 --> 00:18:58.474
And leave, which, of course,
you know, in that day and age...

00:18:58.507 --> 00:19:01.607
So instead, old man isaiah,
well, he gave them all a shave.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:02.607
Kkkch!

00:19:04.874 --> 00:19:06.807
Does it say what happened to the bodies?

00:19:06.841 --> 00:19:08.307
They were all cremated.

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:13.041
Anything else? Yeah.

00:19:13.074 --> 00:19:15.974
Actually, i found a
picture of the family.

00:19:16.007 --> 00:19:17.774
It's right here somewhere.

00:19:17.807 --> 00:19:19.707
Right. Here it is.

00:19:27.807 --> 00:19:30.440
Hey, could we get a
copy of this, please?

00:19:30.474 --> 00:19:32.307
Sure.

00:19:36.407 --> 00:19:37.607
Dad...

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:40.807
You promised you wouldn't
sell that painting.

00:19:40.841 --> 00:19:42.674
I know, sweetie, but evelyn's offered

00:19:42.707 --> 00:19:44.208
A persuasive amount of money.

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:47.774
You're shameless, you know that?

00:19:47.807 --> 00:19:50.574
For that kind of money,
i can afford to be.

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:57.240
Sam: i'm telling you,
man. I'm sure of it.

00:19:57.273 --> 00:19:59.774
The painting at the auction
house, dad is looking down.

00:19:59.807 --> 00:20:01.607
The painting here, dad's looking out.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:02.974
The painting has changed, dean.

00:20:03.007 --> 00:20:05.307
So you think that daddy dearest
is trapped in the painting,

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:06.974
And he's handing out columbian neckties

00:20:07.007 --> 00:20:09.540
Like he did with his family?
Well, yeah, it seems like it.

00:20:09.574 --> 00:20:11.574
But if his bones are already dusted,

00:20:11.607 --> 00:20:13.407
Then how are we gonna stop him?

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:14.774
Well, if isaiah's position changed,

00:20:14.807 --> 00:20:16.874
Then maybe some other things in
the painting changed, as well.

00:20:16.907 --> 00:20:18.273
It could give us some clues.

00:20:18.307 --> 00:20:19.574
Like a "da vinci code" deal?

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:21.674
I don't know.

00:20:21.707 --> 00:20:24.273
I'm still waiting for
the movie on that one.

00:20:24.307 --> 00:20:26.373
Anyway, we got to get back
in and see that painting,

00:20:26.407 --> 00:20:28.440
Which is a good thing,
because you can get more time

00:20:28.474 --> 00:20:29.707
To crush on your girlfriend.

00:20:29.741 --> 00:20:31.974
Dude...enough already.

00:20:32.007 --> 00:20:34.007
What? "What?" Ever since we got here,

00:20:34.041 --> 00:20:36.108
You've been trying to
pimp me out to sarah.

00:20:36.141 --> 00:20:37.340
Just back off, all right?

00:20:37.373 --> 00:20:38.741
Well, you like her, don't you?

00:20:38.774 --> 00:20:40.440
All right, you like her. She likes you.

00:20:40.474 --> 00:20:42.007
You're both consenting adults.

00:20:42.041 --> 00:20:43.108
What's the point, dean?

00:20:43.141 --> 00:20:44.607
We'll just leave. We always leave.

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:46.373
Well, i'm not talking
about marriage, sam.

00:20:46.407 --> 00:20:48.307
I don't get it. What do
you care if i hook up?

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:50.208
Maybe you wouldn't be
so cranky all the time.

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:58.340
Seriously, sam, this isn't
about just hooking up, okay?

00:20:58.373 --> 00:21:01.340
I think that this sarah
girl could be good for you.

00:21:03.741 --> 00:21:07.108
And i don't mean any
disrespect, but i'm -

00:21:07.141 --> 00:21:09.074
I'm sure that this is
about jessica, right?

00:21:10.074 --> 00:21:14.874
Now, i don't know what it's like
to lose somebody like that...

00:21:14.907 --> 00:21:16.774
But...

00:21:16.807 --> 00:21:18.807
I would think that she
would want you to be happy.

00:21:21.108 --> 00:21:24.141
God forbid, have fun once in a while.

00:21:24.174 --> 00:21:25.373
Wouldn't she?

00:21:30.041 --> 00:21:31.807
Yeah, i know she would.

00:21:36.807 --> 00:21:42.240
Yeah, you're right. Part
of this is about jessica.

00:21:42.273 --> 00:21:43.640
But not the main part.

00:21:43.674 --> 00:21:45.574
What's it about?

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:51.707
Yeah, all right.

00:21:51.741 --> 00:21:54.707
Well, we still got to see that painting,

00:21:54.741 --> 00:21:58.108
Which means you still
got to call sarah, so...

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.074
Sarah, hey. It's sam.

00:22:12.108 --> 00:22:13.941
Hey, hi.

00:22:13.974 --> 00:22:16.208
Good, good, yeah. What about you?

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.974
Yeah, good. Good, really good. Smooth.

00:22:19.007 --> 00:22:21.507
So, uh
- So, listen.

00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:23.340
Me and my brother were thinking

00:22:23.373 --> 00:22:25.440
That maybe we'd like to come back in

00:22:25.474 --> 00:22:27.273
And look at the painting again.

00:22:27.307 --> 00:22:29.974
I think maybe we are
interested in buying it.

00:22:30.007 --> 00:22:31.174
Wait, what?

00:22:31.208 --> 00:22:34.307
Who'd you sell it to?

00:22:34.340 --> 00:22:36.841
Sarah, i need an address right now.

00:23:21.974 --> 00:23:23.108
Sam, what's happening?

00:23:23.140 --> 00:23:25.240
I told you you shouldn't have come.

00:23:28.774 --> 00:23:30.008
Hello, anybody home?!

00:23:30.041 --> 00:23:32.574
You said evelyn might be in
danger. What kind of danger?

00:23:32.607 --> 00:23:36.474
I can't knock this sucker
down. I got to pick it.

00:23:36.507 --> 00:23:39.041
What are you guys, burglars?

00:23:39.074 --> 00:23:40.374
I wish it was that simple.

00:23:40.407 --> 00:23:42.841
Look, you really should wait in the car.

00:23:42.874 --> 00:23:44.240
Ugh.

00:23:44.273 --> 00:23:45.741
The hell i will. Evelyn's a friend.

00:23:45.774 --> 00:23:46.807
Evelyn?

00:23:46.841 --> 00:23:48.407
Sam: evelyn!

00:23:53.307 --> 00:23:54.540
Evelyn?

00:24:05.074 --> 00:24:07.741
Evelyn?

00:24:07.774 --> 00:24:09.140
It's sarah blake.

00:24:09.173 --> 00:24:10.607
Are you all right?

00:24:10.641 --> 00:24:11.907
Sarah, don't! Sarah!

00:24:18.008 --> 00:24:20.707
Oh, my god! Oh, my god!

00:24:30.108 --> 00:24:32.874
Hey. You all right?

00:24:32.907 --> 00:24:34.307
No, actually.

00:24:34.340 --> 00:24:37.641
I just lied to the cops and told
them i went to evelyn's alone

00:24:37.674 --> 00:24:40.108
And found her like that.

00:24:40.140 --> 00:24:41.273
Thank you. Don't thank me.

00:24:41.307 --> 00:24:42.674
I'm about to call them right back

00:24:42.707 --> 00:24:44.540
If you don't tell me
what the hell is going on.

00:24:44.574 --> 00:24:46.041
Who's killing these people?

00:24:50.173 --> 00:24:51.741
"What."

00:24:51.774 --> 00:24:53.207
What?

00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:54.474
It's not "who."

00:24:54.507 --> 00:24:57.407
It's "what" is killing those people.

00:25:00.340 --> 00:25:02.907
Sarah, you saw that painting move.

00:25:02.941 --> 00:25:05.741
No.

00:25:05.774 --> 00:25:08.440
No, i was
- I was seeing things.

00:25:08.474 --> 00:25:09.807
It's impossible.

00:25:09.841 --> 00:25:11.507
Yeah, well, welcome to our world.

00:25:11.540 --> 00:25:14.774
Sarah, i know this sounds crazy...

00:25:14.807 --> 00:25:17.041
But we think that that
painting is haunted.

00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:22.941
You're joking.

00:25:27.240 --> 00:25:29.741
You're not joking.

00:25:29.774 --> 00:25:32.207
God, the guys i go out with.

00:25:32.240 --> 00:25:33.874
Sarah, think about it.

00:25:33.907 --> 00:25:37.574
Evelyn, the telescas
- They both had the painting.

00:25:37.607 --> 00:25:39.207
And there have been others before that.

00:25:39.240 --> 00:25:40.774
Wherever this thing goes, people die,

00:25:40.807 --> 00:25:43.173
And we're just trying to stop it...

00:25:43.207 --> 00:25:44.607
And that's the truth.

00:25:44.641 --> 00:25:49.507
Well, then, i guess you better show me.

00:25:49.540 --> 00:25:50.540
I'm coming with you.

00:25:50.574 --> 00:25:51.941
What? No.

00:25:51.974 --> 00:25:54.407
Sarah, no. You should just go home.

00:25:54.440 --> 00:25:57.108
This stuff can get dangerous, and

00:25:59.008 --> 00:26:01.008
And i don't want you to get hurt.

00:26:01.041 --> 00:26:02.907
Look, you guys are probably crazy,

00:26:02.941 --> 00:26:04.474
But if you're right about this,

00:26:04.507 --> 00:26:06.507
When me and my dad sold that painting,

00:26:06.540 --> 00:26:08.540
We might have got these people killed.

00:26:08.574 --> 00:26:11.540
I'm not saying i'm not scared,
'cause i am scared as hell,

00:26:11.574 --> 00:26:13.741
But i'm not gonna run and hide, either.

00:26:16.607 --> 00:26:18.474
So are we going or what?

00:26:18.507 --> 00:26:19.674
Sam

00:26:21.707 --> 00:26:23.041
Marry that girl.

00:26:26.041 --> 00:26:29.874
Uh... isn't this a crime scene?

00:26:29.907 --> 00:26:32.474
You've already lied to the
cops. What's another infraction?

00:26:51.607 --> 00:26:55.207
Aren't you worried that it's
gonna, you know, kill us?

00:26:55.240 --> 00:26:57.407
No, it seems to do its thing at night.

00:26:57.440 --> 00:26:58.874
I think we're all right in daylight.

00:27:03.907 --> 00:27:06.140
Sam, check it out.

00:27:06.173 --> 00:27:07.607
The razor
- It's closed in this one,

00:27:07.641 --> 00:27:09.607
But it's open in that one.
What are you guys looking for?

00:27:09.641 --> 00:27:11.374
If the spirit's changing
aspects of the painting,

00:27:11.407 --> 00:27:14.140
Maybe it's doing so for a reason.

00:27:14.173 --> 00:27:18.374
Hey, hey, look at this
- The painting in the painting.

00:27:23.108 --> 00:27:25.774
It looks like a crypt or
a mausoleum or something.

00:27:36.574 --> 00:27:37.807
"Merchant."

00:27:46.540 --> 00:27:49.207
This is the third
boneyard we've checked.

00:27:49.240 --> 00:27:52.474
This ghost is jerking us around.

00:27:52.507 --> 00:27:55.440
So, this is what you
guys do for a living?

00:27:55.474 --> 00:27:58.008
Not exactly.

00:27:58.041 --> 00:28:00.474
We don't get paid.

00:28:00.507 --> 00:28:03.074
Well, mazel tov.

00:28:04.674 --> 00:28:06.807
Over there.

00:28:41.707 --> 00:28:45.874
Okay, that right there is the
creepiest thing i've ever seen.

00:28:45.907 --> 00:28:48.741
It was sort of a tradition at the time.

00:28:48.774 --> 00:28:49.974
Whenever a child died,

00:28:50.008 --> 00:28:52.240
Sometimes they'd preserve
the kid's favorite toy

00:28:52.273 --> 00:28:55.074
In a glass case, put it next
to the headstone in the crypt.

00:29:00.707 --> 00:29:02.474
Notice anything strange here?

00:29:02.507 --> 00:29:03.974
Uh, where do i start?

00:29:04.008 --> 00:29:05.540
No, that's not what i mean.

00:29:05.574 --> 00:29:06.641
Look at the urns.

00:29:08.907 --> 00:29:10.841
Yeah, there are only four.

00:29:10.874 --> 00:29:13.074
Mom and the three kids.

00:29:13.108 --> 00:29:14.807
Daddy dearest isn't here.

00:29:17.074 --> 00:29:18.574
So where is he?

00:29:18.607 --> 00:29:21.207
Sarah: so, what exactly is
your brother doing in there?

00:29:21.240 --> 00:29:23.074
Searching county death certificates,

00:29:23.108 --> 00:29:25.674
Trying to find out what
happened to isaiah's body.

00:29:25.707 --> 00:29:27.307
How'd he even get in the door?

00:29:27.340 --> 00:29:31.741
Lying and subterfuge, mostly.

00:29:33.941 --> 00:29:37.240
You have a, um
- You have an eyelash on your...

00:29:37.273 --> 00:29:39.074
You have it right
- No. Uh, you know what?

00:29:41.140 --> 00:29:42.440
Do you mind if i -

00:29:42.474 --> 00:29:44.841
No. Okay.

00:29:44.874 --> 00:29:46.841
Okay, i got it.

00:29:46.874 --> 00:29:47.941
Make a wish.

00:29:56.173 --> 00:29:57.574
Sam, can i ask you something?

00:29:57.607 --> 00:30:00.240
Yeah, sure. I don't mean to be forward,

00:30:00.273 --> 00:30:04.941
But a girl could wait here forever.

00:30:04.974 --> 00:30:08.974
Is there something here
between us, or am i delusional?

00:30:09.008 --> 00:30:11.041
You're not delusional.

00:30:11.074 --> 00:30:14.140
But there's a "but" coming.

00:30:14.173 --> 00:30:17.240
But...

00:30:17.273 --> 00:30:19.841
I don't think this would be a good idea.

00:30:21.907 --> 00:30:23.041
Can i ask why?

00:30:25.108 --> 00:30:26.273
'Cause i like you.

00:30:28.674 --> 00:30:30.674
Wait. You lost me.

00:30:33.074 --> 00:30:35.807
Look, it's hard to explain.

00:30:35.841 --> 00:30:40.307
It's just that when
people are around me...

00:30:40.340 --> 00:30:42.074
I don't know, they get hurt.

00:30:42.108 --> 00:30:43.140
What do you mean?

00:30:43.173 --> 00:30:46.407
I mean, like, physically hurt.

00:30:46.440 --> 00:30:49.474
With what my brother and i do, it's...

00:30:54.941 --> 00:30:58.240
Sarah...

00:30:58.273 --> 00:31:00.240
I had a girlfriend.

00:31:01.641 --> 00:31:04.041
And she died.

00:31:04.074 --> 00:31:07.807
And my mom died, too.

00:31:07.841 --> 00:31:11.841
I don't know, it's like...

00:31:11.874 --> 00:31:15.074
It's like i'm cursed or something...

00:31:15.108 --> 00:31:16.707
Like death just follows me around.

00:31:16.741 --> 00:31:19.273
Look, i'm not scared of much,

00:31:19.307 --> 00:31:21.774
But if i let myself have
feelings for anybody -

00:31:21.807 --> 00:31:23.674
You're scared they get hurt, too.

00:31:25.574 --> 00:31:30.474
That's very sweet and very archaic.

00:31:30.507 --> 00:31:32.008
Sorry? Look, i'm a big girl, sam.

00:31:32.041 --> 00:31:34.474
It's not your job to
make decisions for me.

00:31:34.507 --> 00:31:36.807
There's always a chance of getting hurt.

00:31:36.841 --> 00:31:38.540
I'm not talking about a broken heart

00:31:38.574 --> 00:31:39.707
And a tub of haagen-Dazs.

00:31:39.741 --> 00:31:40.907
I'm talking about life and death.

00:31:40.941 --> 00:31:42.974
And tomorrow, i could get hit by a bus.

00:31:43.008 --> 00:31:44.108
That's what life is.

00:31:45.173 --> 00:31:48.540
Look, i know losing somebody you love
- It's terrible.

00:31:48.574 --> 00:31:53.108
You shut yourself off.
Believe me, i know.

00:31:53.140 --> 00:31:55.807
But when you shut out pain...

00:31:55.841 --> 00:31:58.041
You shut out everything else, too.

00:31:58.074 --> 00:32:01.641
Sarah, you don't understand.
The pain that i went through...

00:32:01.674 --> 00:32:06.207
I can't go through it again. I can't.

00:32:10.240 --> 00:32:11.874
Am i interrupting something?

00:32:11.907 --> 00:32:13.707
No. Not at all.

00:32:13.741 --> 00:32:15.108
Apparently.

00:32:15.140 --> 00:32:16.941
So, what'd you get? Pay dirt.

00:32:16.974 --> 00:32:20.374
Apparently, the surviving
relatives of the merchant family

00:32:20.407 --> 00:32:22.907
Were so ashamed of isaiah that
they didn't want him interred

00:32:22.941 --> 00:32:25.273
With the family, so they
handed him over to the county.

00:32:25.307 --> 00:32:27.374
The county gave him a pauper's funeral,

00:32:27.407 --> 00:32:28.807
Economy-Style.

00:32:28.841 --> 00:32:31.074
Turns out he wasn't cremated.
He was buried in a pine box.

00:32:31.108 --> 00:32:32.540
<i>So there are bones to burn.</i>

00:32:32.574 --> 00:32:34.974
There are bones to burn.
Tell me you know where.

00:32:48.641 --> 00:32:50.574
You guys seem to be

00:32:50.607 --> 00:32:52.707
Uncomfortably comfortable with this.

00:32:52.741 --> 00:32:57.240
Well...this isn't exactly
the first grave we dug.

00:32:57.273 --> 00:33:01.574
Still think i'm a catch?

00:33:03.008 --> 00:33:05.074
Think i got something.

00:33:31.140 --> 00:33:32.974
Dean: you been a real
pain in the ass, isaiah.

00:33:35.008 --> 00:33:36.641
Good riddance.

00:33:48.140 --> 00:33:49.874
Dean, keep the motor running.

00:33:49.907 --> 00:33:52.707
I thought the painting was harmless now.

00:33:52.741 --> 00:33:55.507
Better safe than sorry.
We're gonna bury the sucker.

00:33:55.540 --> 00:33:56.641
I want to come with you.

00:33:56.674 --> 00:33:58.273
Are you sure?

00:33:58.307 --> 00:34:00.008
Hey, hey, hey.

00:34:00.041 --> 00:34:02.607
I'll stay here. You go make your move.

00:34:02.641 --> 00:34:04.474
S- S-Sam,
i'm serious!

00:34:31.874 --> 00:34:34.173
Uh, sam...

00:34:34.207 --> 00:34:36.941
You're the expert on
all this ghost stuff.

00:34:36.974 --> 00:34:38.374
Is that painting supposed
to look like that?

00:34:40.907 --> 00:34:43.008
Where's the little girl?

00:34:45.540 --> 00:34:46.974
And the razor?

00:35:01.941 --> 00:35:04.641
Dean! Hey, is that you?!

00:35:04.674 --> 00:35:06.140
Dean: sammy, you all right?!

00:35:11.340 --> 00:35:12.941
Tell me you slammed the front door.

00:35:12.974 --> 00:35:14.674
No, it wasn't me. I think
it was the little girl.

00:35:14.707 --> 00:35:16.774
Girl? What girl? Yeah,
she's out of the painting.

00:35:16.807 --> 00:35:18.307
I think it might have
been her all along.

00:35:18.340 --> 00:35:19.674
Wasn't the dad looking down at her?

00:35:19.707 --> 00:35:21.140
Maybe he was trying to warn us.

00:35:21.173 --> 00:35:23.574
Hey, let's recap later.
Just get us out of here.

00:35:23.607 --> 00:35:26.407
I'm trying to pick the lock, and
the door won't budge. Break it down.

00:35:26.440 --> 00:35:29.407
Okay, genius, let me grab my battering
ram! Dean, the damn thing's coming!

00:35:29.440 --> 00:35:31.574
You're gonna have to hold it
off until i figure something out.

00:35:31.607 --> 00:35:33.574
Get some salt or iron.

00:35:36.707 --> 00:35:38.907
What kind of house doesn't have salt?

00:35:38.941 --> 00:35:41.407
Hey, you find any
iron? No, what's it for?

00:35:41.440 --> 00:35:43.307
Iron repels evil spirits,
but it's got to be pure.

00:35:43.340 --> 00:35:45.574
Hurry.

00:35:45.607 --> 00:35:49.173
Uh, dean, give me a
sec. Don't go anywhere.

00:35:49.207 --> 00:35:51.707
Look at a chair. Sometimes the seats...

00:36:10.574 --> 00:36:11.674
Sam!

00:36:29.574 --> 00:36:31.874
That is just so wrong.

00:36:53.273 --> 00:36:56.108
Iron?

00:36:56.140 --> 00:36:57.173
Yeah.

00:36:57.207 --> 00:36:59.540
Sam, are you okay?

00:36:59.574 --> 00:37:00.574
Yeah, for now.

00:37:00.607 --> 00:37:01.974
How we gonna waste her?

00:37:02.008 --> 00:37:03.774
I don't know. She was already cremated.

00:37:03.807 --> 00:37:06.041
There's nothing left to burn.
Well, then, how's she still around?

00:37:06.074 --> 00:37:07.440
There must be something else.

00:37:08.741 --> 00:37:10.240
Sam, wait.

00:37:10.273 --> 00:37:12.440
We used to handle antique
dolls at the auction.

00:37:12.474 --> 00:37:15.540
Well, that's fascinating,
sarah, but important right now?

00:37:15.574 --> 00:37:18.707
Back then, they used to make
the dolls in the kid's image.

00:37:18.741 --> 00:37:19.941
I mean, everything.

00:37:19.974 --> 00:37:22.407
Like, they would use
the kid's real hair.

00:37:22.440 --> 00:37:23.607
Dean?

00:37:23.641 --> 00:37:26.574
Sarah says the doll might
have the girl's hair.

00:37:26.607 --> 00:37:29.574
Human remains
- Same as bones.

00:37:29.607 --> 00:37:31.440
Both: the mausoleum.

00:38:00.207 --> 00:38:01.974
Sam!

00:38:26.974 --> 00:38:27.974
Come on, dean.

00:38:48.207 --> 00:38:50.140
Come on! Come on!

00:39:42.240 --> 00:39:43.474
Sam, you good?

00:39:47.607 --> 00:39:48.674
Not bad.

00:40:07.524 --> 00:40:09.958
This was archived in the county records.

00:40:09.991 --> 00:40:12.524
The merchant's adopted
daughter, melanie.

00:40:12.557 --> 00:40:14.123
Know why she was up for adoption?

00:40:14.157 --> 00:40:17.024
'Cause her real family
was murdered in their beds.

00:40:17.058 --> 00:40:18.290
She killed them?

00:40:18.324 --> 00:40:20.058
Yeah, who would suspect
her? A sweet little girl.

00:40:20.090 --> 00:40:22.290
So then she kills isaiah and his family.

00:40:22.324 --> 00:40:23.791
The old man takes the blame.

00:40:23.824 --> 00:40:26.024
His spirit's been trying
to warn people ever since.

00:40:26.058 --> 00:40:27.724
Where's this one go?

00:40:27.757 --> 00:40:29.357
Take it out back and burn it.

00:40:31.290 --> 00:40:34.757
I'm serious, guys. Thanks.

00:40:37.490 --> 00:40:39.624
So, why'd the girl do it?

00:40:39.657 --> 00:40:41.624
Killing others, killing herself -

00:40:41.657 --> 00:40:43.691
Some people are just born tortured.

00:40:43.724 --> 00:40:46.390
So when they die, their
spirits are just as dark.

00:40:46.424 --> 00:40:48.657
Maybe. I don't really care. It's over.

00:40:48.691 --> 00:40:51.324
We move on.

00:40:53.157 --> 00:40:54.757
I guess this means you're leaving.

00:41:01.524 --> 00:41:05.457
I'll go wait in the car. See you, sarah.

00:41:09.757 --> 00:41:11.924
I'm the one who burned the
doll and destroyed the spirit,

00:41:11.958 --> 00:41:13.157
But don't thank me or anything.

00:41:19.190 --> 00:41:22.524
There are a million things
that i want to say to you,

00:41:22.557 --> 00:41:25.457
But for the life of me,
i can't think of one.

00:41:25.490 --> 00:41:28.390
Yeah, i'll miss you, too.

00:41:28.424 --> 00:41:30.924
You know, there's a
lesson in all of this.

00:41:30.958 --> 00:41:31.958
What's that?

00:41:31.991 --> 00:41:34.591
We all got through this in one piece.

00:41:35.691 --> 00:41:37.290
I didn't get hurt.

00:41:37.324 --> 00:41:39.324
Yeah, i'm glad for that.

00:41:39.357 --> 00:41:42.724
So maybe you're not cursed.

00:41:42.757 --> 00:41:45.223
Maybe...

00:41:48.557 --> 00:41:51.024
Maybe you'll come back and see me.

00:41:54.691 --> 00:41:56.257
I will.

00:42:40.058 --> 00:42:42.691
That's my boy.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
